How many samples is enough?

Step-by-step calculation

\bar{x} \pm \left(t_{n-1} \times \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}\right)


Calculate the sample mean, \bar{x}
Calculate the sample standard deviation, s
Determine the standard error of the mean, SE_{\bar{x}} = \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
Look up the t-critical value, t_{n-1}, for 95% confidence and n - 1 degrees of freedom
Compute the margin of error: \text{ME} = t_{n-1} \times SE_{\bar{x}}
The 95% CI is: \bar{x} \pm \text{ME}


You need to be able to calculate this by hand or with a calculator.

